    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d529">

                <pb facs="0532" n="448" sameAs="frus:frus1918Supp02/pg448"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 863.852/13</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in Switzerland</hi> (<hi
                        rendition="#italic">Stovall</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary
                        of State </hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#center">[Telegram]</seg>
                </opener>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Berne</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1917-04-17">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">April 17, 1917</hi></date>. <lb/> [<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Received 4.20 p.m.</hi>]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>779. Replying No. 1644, 7th April. For Phelps Bros, [from Austro-Americana]:</p>
                <p>Approve your action for our boats. You have authority together with Buenos Aires
                    without referring any more to us to sell best possible all our other steamers,
                    namely <hi rendition="#italic"> Martha, Virginia, Laura, Alice</hi>. Instruct
                    our captains to cooperate fully with you. Provide for them, officers, and whole
                    crew adequate board and continue payments as heretofore unless you secure them
                    adequate employment. Cable name of European bankers who will pay us. Working on
                    Tripcovich, Atlantica, and Orient steamers and cabling later [regarding]
                    Austro-Americana crew.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Stovall</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
